I squashed your commits into one, rebased on 8.2, and added a commit on top: the name was stated twice in a service definition, as the `$name` argument and in the tag, and `RegisterBlindIndexesPass` only checked the tag, so two services tagged apart but deriving under one name would tag a value alike again. The pass now hands the name of the tag to the `$name` argument and refuses a service stating another one. The bridge README states the name once, and builds the wrapped key as a `Ciphertext`, which the `%env()%` string it passed is not. I also updated the description.
